01:14:40.880 --> 01:14:43.310
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: DOLE and together with the labor force

asr-001005
01:14:43.320 --> 01:14:45.950
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: we signed already and they play a very

asr-001006
01:14:45.960 --> 01:14:49.750
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: big part in our letter C,

asr-001007
01:14:49.760 --> 01:14:51.950
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: centralized human capital development

asr-001008
01:14:51.960 --> 01:14:54.350
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: because they give us the number.

asr-001009
01:14:54.360 --> 01:14:56.150
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We relay it to the SUCs.

asr-001010
01:14:56.160 --> 01:14:57.300
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Ito lang ang kukunin ninyo

asr-001011
01:14:57.300 --> 01:14:58.000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: in agriculture

asr-001012
01:14:58.000 --> 01:14:58.550
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: and so on and so on.

asr-001015
01:14:58.560 --> 01:15:00.050
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Chairperson.

asr-001016
01:15:00.050 --> 01:15:12.910
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Sa 2027 budget po, ano ang component ng CHED para i-implement ang Labor Education Act? Kung meron po, kindly discuss it, Madam Chairperson.

asr-001017
01:15:20.980 --> 01:15:41.780
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah, kasama po sa aming, I'm just scanning my notes, kasama po siya sa MNE Higher Education Program na hindi binigay is 258 million. So, this may be one na masasagasaan kung hindi po ibibigay ito.

asr-001018
01:15:42.310 --> 01:15:49.630
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Chairperson, for pointing that out. So, kailangan po natin na pondohan ang implementation ng Labor Education Act.

asr-001019
01:15:50.640 --> 01:16:08.900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Sa roll-out plan po for academic year 2026-2027, ang labor education po ay dinideliver as a 12-hour component embedded in NSTP or GE courses. Meron po bang plano ang CHED na i-expand ang labor education as a stand-alone credit-bearing subject?

asr-001020
01:16:11.940 --> 01:16:22.980
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po. Immediately after we jointly signed with DOLE, ay meron na kaming two implementation big-ticket tracks. One is curriculum integration.

asr-001021
01:16:22.980 --> 01:16:42.680
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And the other one is the institutional implementation. So, may mga degree program po kasi na nag-consult kami na baka hindi pwedeng i-integrate sa curriculum, so ginag-incorporate sa NSTP.

asr-001022
01:16:43.100 --> 01:16:51.460
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Chairperson. Now, moving on, on TFI policy, RA 6728, Section 5.

asr-001023
01:16:52.160 --> 01:16:53.500
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Ano po 'yun, RA?

asr-001024
01:16:55.220 --> 01:17:10.900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: RA 6728, Section 5. So, that's the GASP law. 70% ng tuition fees ay dapat pumapunta sa mga manggagawa sa mga educational institutions. Aware po ba kayo dito, Madam Chairperson?

asr-001025
01:17:11.100 --> 01:17:18.660
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po. We develop a good equation so that it will be inclusive and equitable across region. We have the data, Honorable.

asr-001026
01:17:18.720 --> 01:17:32.440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ngayon po ang problema dito, Madam Chairperson, in practice, hindi po ito ginagawa ng mga private HEIs. What is very explicit in the law, hindi po pinapatupad ng mga private HEIs.

asr-001027
01:17:32.440 --> 01:17:43.220
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So whenever there is a tuition fee increase, hindi nakukuha ng mga manggagawa sa mga private HEIs yung 70% share nila. Would you care to comment on this, Madam Chairperson?

asr-001028
01:17:58.380 --> 01:17:59.600
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Can I ask a friend?

asr-001029
01:17:59.900 --> 01:18:00.940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Yes po, Madam Chairperson.

asr-001030
01:18:00.940 --> 01:18:16.360
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May I? Kasi best na ibubulong niya sa akin, sasabihin nilang, but as an introduction po, I met already the heads and officials of the higher education institution in the office regarding the tuition fee increase.

asr-001031
01:18:17.440 --> 01:18:28.980
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: In fact, before the crisis, the oil crisis in the Middle East, pumunta po sila sa amin and I thank them because they listened to us.

asr-001032
01:18:28.980 --> 01:18:36.860
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Let us comply with the EO, the President, and the memorandum order to hold the tuition fee increase.

asr-001033
01:18:37.280 --> 01:18:43.840
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: But before we give the permission for the increase, we have criteria to be met.

asr-001034
01:18:44.720 --> 01:19:01.980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Yes po, Madam Chair. Ang tanong ko po is, hindi po doon patungkol kung meron bang tuition fee increase o wala. Ang tanong ko po is, bakit hindi nakukuha ng mga teachers, staff, yung 70% share nila sa tuition fee increase?

asr-001035
01:19:02.395 --> 01:19:02.615
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Okay.

asr-001036
01:19:02.615 --> 01:19:15.240
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: And whenever these staff will go to CHED, ang sinasabi po palagi ng CHED, refer to your respective management for appropriate action. So I would like to get the clarification of CHED regarding this.

asr-001037
01:19:16.120 --> 01:19:33.820
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Part of the signed documents by the private higher education when we give the final clearance for tuition fee is a certification to comply with the provision of RA 6728, Section 5.

asr-001038
01:19:34.480 --> 01:19:37.400
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Nagsa-sign po naman sila.

asr-001039
01:19:38.080 --> 01:19:57.880
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Unfortunately, I do not know, correct me if I'm wrong, that we have not received any complaint from the faculty in charge. Have we received? Or even, we have the e-Tugon, Congressman. We have already strengthened our online e-Tugon system. You please go to CHED website.

asr-001040
01:20:00.080 --> 01:20:06.280
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Chairperson, ang Council of Teachers and Staffs of Colleges and Universities of the Philippines, COTESCO.

asr-001041
01:20:06.280 --> 01:20:13.260
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: This is the biggest alliance. Lagi pong pumupunta sa CHED. Specifically, CEU-FAO.

asr-001042
01:20:25.580 --> 01:20:43.220
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ito, Madam Chair, there is a communication from CHED na sinasabi po dito na refer na lang to the management regarding this matter. And this is happening elsewhere po sa mga private HEIs natin.

asr-001043
01:20:44.340 --> 01:20:48.680
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah, we will. Ikaw na lang. We will address this.

asr-001044
01:20:48.880 --> 01:21:07.440
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We will address this. And I am told that Director Corr is the Director of the Student Services. May I be permitted to give the answer more detailed, Honorable Congressman?

asr-001045
01:21:08.140 --> 01:21:13.580
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Yes, please introduce yourself lang. Kahit doon ka na lang before you proceed to answer. Thank you.

asr-001046
01:21:16.080 --> 01:21:21.560
CHED Director Corinna Frances Cabanilla: Good afternoon po. I am Cor Cabanilla, the Director of Office of Student Development and Services.

asr-001047
01:21:22.300 --> 01:21:32.840
CHED Director Corinna Frances Cabanilla: Regarding your concern, we are already talking with COTESCO on the matter. We received their concern and we immediately have a scheduled meeting with them.

asr-001048
01:21:34.640 --> 01:21:46.560
CHED Director Corinna Frances Cabanilla: We understand as well that it is a labor concern. So to facilitate the matter, we will just help them coordinate with the Department of Labor and Employment

asr-001049
01:21:46.560 --> 01:21:50.120
CHED Director Corinna Frances Cabanilla: so that we also do not cross any jurisdiction pertaining to the matter.

asr-001051
01:21:50.120 --> 01:21:55.480
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Yes, we understand that it is a labor issue, but it is also within your mandate.

asr-001052
01:21:56.360 --> 01:22:05.340
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Section 9.2, 9.3, 9.4 of Memorandum Order No. 3, Series of 2012, duty po ng CHED.

asr-001053
01:22:05.700 --> 01:22:14.160
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Okay, ako na. Thank you very much for reminding us this, Congressman. We will look into this immediately.

asr-001054
01:22:14.600 --> 01:22:15.960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Chairperson.

asr-001057
01:22:22.340 --> 01:22:26.420
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We will, because we already signed memorandum.

asr-001058
01:22:26.420 --> 01:22:29.620
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Chairperson. My next question would be on the MORPHE.

asr-001059
01:22:31.400 --> 01:22:45.760
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Sabi niyo po, last year, 360 days na nakalipas. 100 days, on your first 100 days ay a-address niyo po itong MORPHE. Ano na po ang status dito, Madam Chairperson?

asr-001060
01:22:50.920 --> 01:22:53.320
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We already have the draft.

asr-001062
01:23:00.220 --> 01:23:11.860
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah, the promise is not tabled. It's not tabled. We immediately form a technical working group across SUC to review all our policies.

asr-001063
01:23:11.860 --> 01:23:18.080
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: As I mentioned earlier, there are 1,000-plus policies which have never been reviewed in the past.

asr-001064
01:23:18.080 --> 01:23:26.460
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: But because of the limited number of personnel in CHED, we tap the best lawyers across SUCs. And one of this is MORPHE already.

asr-001065
01:23:27.260 --> 01:23:33.060
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So we already have a comprehensive revision of the Manual of Regulation of Private Higher Education,

asr-001066
01:23:33.580 --> 01:23:40.560
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: updating the primary regulatory instrument governing private higher education institutions to reflect.

asr-001067
01:23:40.560 --> 01:23:52.840
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And as of last meeting in our CEB, we will have the last scheduled consultation, Honorable Congressman, on September 15 to 17.

asr-001068
01:23:53.240 --> 01:24:01.680
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We will present our draft and after such getting input of the private higher education, we will be able to publish them.

asr-001072
01:24:01.820 --> 01:24:06.440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maraming salamat po, Madam Chairperson. Maganda po na nabanggit niyo na meron na pong tentative schedule.

asr-001073
01:24:07.160 --> 01:24:16.180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Dahil po mula October 23, 2025, that's the preliminary meeting for MORPHE review and the second meeting was done on November 19, 2025.

asr-001074
01:24:16.680 --> 01:24:22.960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Hindi pa po nakakuha ng update yung COTESCO, but it is good na sinabi niyo po na meron nang tentative schedule.

asr-001075
01:24:23.320 --> 01:24:26.700
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Chairperson, alam niyo po kung bakit ko binibigyan din ito?

asr-001076
01:24:26.860 --> 01:24:31.100
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Dahil yung MORPHE is in direct violation of the Labor Code.

asr-001077
01:24:31.760 --> 01:24:35.480
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Inadmit niyo rin po ito ng CHED during the last budget hearing.

asr-001078
01:24:35.980 --> 01:24:40.680
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Malinaw sa Labor Code, ang probationary period is six months only.

asr-001079
01:24:40.960 --> 01:24:45.340
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pero dito sa MORPHE, six consecutive semesters.

asr-001080
01:24:46.340 --> 01:24:53.740
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ibig sabihin, ang probationary period for workers in private HEIs ay tatlong taon.

asr-001081
01:24:53.740 --> 01:25:00.980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So malinaw na sinusupersede ng MORPHE yung nakasulat sa ating Labor Code.

asr-001082
01:25:01.120 --> 01:25:08.200
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kaya maganda po na ito ay mapag-usapan na natin dahil ginagamit po ito, Madam Chairperson,

asr-001083
01:25:08.500 --> 01:25:16.800
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ng mga private higher educational institutions para perpetually hindi ma-regular yung kanilang mga faculty.

asr-001084
01:25:16.800 --> 01:25:23.340
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: At ginagamit din po nila ito bilang paraan para arbitrarily tanggalin na lang sila

asr-001085
01:25:23.340 --> 01:25:26.860
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: o i-deload o hindi na pagturuin doon sa mga private HEIs.

asr-001086
01:25:27.340 --> 01:25:31.980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Makukuha po ba namin ng commitment ng Commission on Higher Education regarding this, Madam Chairperson?

asr-001087
01:25:32.360 --> 01:25:40.440
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: I will personally monitor the final draft, Honorable Congressman, after September 15 to 17.

asr-001088
01:25:40.640 --> 01:25:41.840
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And we will update you gladly.

asr-001089
01:25:42.280 --> 01:25:44.240
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Maraming salamat po, Madam Chairperson.

asr-001090
01:25:44.440 --> 01:25:45.160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-001091
01:25:45.780 --> 01:25:47.920
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Thank you, the Honorable San Fernando.

asr-001092
01:25:48.140 --> 01:25:52.340
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: And now, from the majority, the Chair recognizes the Honorable Jude Acidre.

asr-001093
01:25:53.180 --> 01:25:54.340
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-001094
01:25:54.640 --> 01:26:01.500
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Magandang umaga po, Chairman Agrupis, at sa mga kasamahan niyo po niya sa Commission on Higher Education.

asr-001095
01:26:02.740 --> 01:26:08.740
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Isa po sa centerpiece po ng higher education reform po natin, ang free higher education.

asr-001096
01:26:09.220 --> 01:26:20.500
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: At nagpapasalamat po tayo sa CHED na bagamat pansin naman po natin yung kakulangan sa resources at sa budget,

asr-001097
01:26:20.680 --> 01:26:23.160
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: patuloy na pinapatupad ng CHED.

asr-001098
01:26:23.160 --> 01:26:27.700
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: At nag-administrasyong ito ang pagbibigay prioridad sa education.

asr-001099
01:26:28.600 --> 01:26:33.180
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Madam Chair, base po sa datos na meron po na-present po ninyo,

asr-001100
01:26:34.600 --> 01:26:42.020
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: lumalabas po sa parating na school year na may kakulangan po na 28 billion sa UAQTEA,

asr-001101
01:26:43.200 --> 01:26:50.300
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: of which 92 billion, 92.2 billion, dapat para sa FHE

asr-001102
01:26:50.300 --> 01:26:54.840
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: at 18.4 billion ay para po sa TES.

asr-001103
01:26:56.800 --> 01:27:04.780
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Nangangahulugan po na 137,000 students ang hindi po makaka-avail ng free higher education

asr-001104
01:27:04.780 --> 01:27:12.560
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: at around 833,000 students naman ang mawawala sa TES.

asr-001105
01:27:14.020 --> 01:27:19.720
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Nababahala po ako dito, Madam Chair, bagamat naintindihan ko yung limitasyon ng fiscal space,

asr-001106
01:27:20.880 --> 01:27:27.580
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: kasi mukha pong magkakaroon po tayo dahil sa funding cap ng free higher education,

asr-001107
01:27:29.720 --> 01:27:38.900
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: eh mukhang mapipilitan po ang ating mga SUC na tumanggap lamang ng mga estudyante na pasok po sa pondong nakalaan sa kanila.

asr-001108
01:27:38.900 --> 01:27:49.040
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: At naaalala po ako kasi if this becomes a pattern, ang lalabas po nito magkakaroon po ng progressive na decrease

asr-001109
01:27:49.040 --> 01:27:52.780
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: in the absorptive capacity ang ating mga SUCs.

asr-001110
01:27:53.900 --> 01:27:57.540
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Alam ko na ho na obvious na ang rason ay lakihan ho ng pondo,

asr-001111
01:27:57.900 --> 01:28:09.060
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: pero ano po kaya ang mga rekomendasyon ng CHED sa kongresong ito para madagdagan po natin ang absorptive capacity ng ating mga SUCs?

asr-001112
01:28:10.060 --> 01:28:10.960
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Madam Chair.

asr-001113
01:28:13.060 --> 01:28:16.920
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah, napakabigat po ang tanong na yan kong,

asr-001114
01:28:16.920 --> 01:28:18.700
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: but as our...

asr-001115
01:28:18.700 --> 01:28:22.640
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: our mandate now, we always go back to the data.

asr-001116
01:28:23.720 --> 01:28:30.480
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So, nag-umpisa kaming nag-collect ng data, ng initial simulation, no, ng 541 SUC.

asr-001117
01:28:31.260 --> 01:28:33.680
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Ito yung data po, bago ko sagutin yun.

asr-001118
01:28:34.560 --> 01:28:40.580
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: There are, of the 541 state, university, and colleges, including their campuses,

asr-001119
01:28:41.660 --> 01:28:46.580
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: 68% po exceeded their estimated enrollment capacity.

asr-001120
01:28:47.260 --> 01:28:48.440
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Bakit kaya?

asr-001121
01:28:48.440 --> 01:28:53.120
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Siguro naaawa sila, or talagang kailangan nilang i-cover.

asr-001122
01:28:53.880 --> 01:28:59.620
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yung 32% within or below their estimated enrollment capacity po.

asr-001123
01:29:00.140 --> 01:29:04.000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Now, nag-agree na po kami ng student-faculty ratio.

asr-001124
01:29:04.520 --> 01:29:08.060
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kung iano namin yung faculty insufficient, so,

asr-001125
01:29:08.180 --> 01:29:10.980
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: ang rason po ng aming...

asr-001126
01:29:12.400 --> 01:29:17.200
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: because of this data, we already sit down, in fact, with the...

asr-001127
01:29:18.780 --> 01:29:21.900
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Department of Budget, to come up with an equation,

asr-001128
01:29:23.560 --> 01:29:28.300
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: basing on the 1 is to 40 faculty-student ratio.

asr-001129
01:29:29.540 --> 01:29:35.540
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So, meron na po kaming number, and we are trying to implement this.

asr-001130
01:29:35.540 --> 01:29:39.300
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Ito lang yung capacity ninyo, ito lang muna ang kukunin ninyo.

asr-001131
01:29:39.320 --> 01:29:47.440
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: But through the years, based on the data, kahit sinabi na noon na you only enroll yung kaya nyo,

asr-001132
01:29:47.500 --> 01:29:48.680
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: they keep admitting.

asr-001134
01:29:49.200 --> 01:29:52.200
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So, ang recommendation na number one po,

asr-001135
01:29:52.200 --> 01:29:58.060
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: in as much as we are increasing the classroom of our...

asr-001137
01:29:58.060 --> 01:30:02.140
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: basic education, we really need

asr-001138
01:30:02.140 --> 01:30:04.480
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: to give attention to the increase

asr-001139
01:30:04.480 --> 01:30:06.620
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: in the classroom of our

asr-001140
01:30:06.620 --> 01:30:08.360
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: higher education. Kasi po

asr-001141
01:30:08.440 --> 01:30:10.300
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: kung mas madaming classroom ang DepEd,

asr-001142
01:30:10.540 --> 01:30:11.240
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: mas madaming graduate,

asr-001143
01:30:12.380 --> 01:30:14.680
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: pero hindi ginalaw ang infrastructure

asr-001144
01:30:14.680 --> 01:30:16.080
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: ng higher ed, saan po

asr-001145
01:30:16.080 --> 01:30:17.600
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: namin sila ikukulong?

asr-001146
01:30:18.320 --> 01:30:20.260
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: That's number one question po. Number two

asr-001147
01:30:20.260 --> 01:30:21.900
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: po, is the faculty.

asr-001148
01:30:23.100 --> 01:30:23.800
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Faculty items.

asr-001149
01:30:25.000 --> 01:30:26.360
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So, kung

asr-001150
01:30:26.360 --> 01:30:27.960
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: ang existing enrollment nila

asr-001151
01:30:27.960 --> 01:30:29.880
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: is beyond the 1 is to

asr-001152
01:30:29.880 --> 01:30:31.860
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: 40 faculty-student

asr-001153
01:30:31.860 --> 01:30:34.180
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: ratio, ang sasagot

asr-001154
01:30:34.180 --> 01:30:36.080
