04:20:57.740 --> 04:21:03.520
Rep. Brian Poe: One is the efficiency of government scholarships and the second is financial literacy.

asr-004690
04:21:03.920 --> 04:21:11.260
Rep. Brian Poe: You are immediately teaching students how to open a bank account, how to save money and how to maintain a bank account.

asr-004691
04:21:11.440 --> 04:21:13.300
Rep. Brian Poe: We are banking the unbanked.

asr-004692
04:21:13.300 --> 04:21:18.060
Rep. Brian Poe: We're creating another generation of students who now know how to save money.

asr-004693
04:21:18.680 --> 04:21:25.140
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Chair, this is a very important step forward for Ched and I believe we should continue to support it.

asr-004694
04:21:25.140 --> 04:21:38.360
Rep. Brian Poe: I also saw that in your budget, you have a 214% increase, I believe, or sorry, a 150% increase in the budget for the Bagong Pilipinas Merit Scholarship.

asr-004695
04:21:38.360 --> 04:21:38.820
Rep. Brian Poe: Is this correct?

asr-004696
04:21:41.740 --> 04:21:42.420
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po.

asr-004697
04:21:43.540 --> 04:21:46.100
Rep. Brian Poe: Can you tell me a little bit about this program?

asr-004698
04:21:46.240 --> 04:21:50.120
Rep. Brian Poe: I believe, obviously, it's for our merit scholars, our top performing students.

asr-004699
04:21:50.480 --> 04:21:52.660
Rep. Brian Poe: How many students are supported by this program?

asr-004700
04:21:53.680 --> 04:21:54.200
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah.

asr-004701
04:21:54.280 --> 04:21:55.100
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Thank you very much.

asr-004702
04:21:55.220 --> 04:22:00.500
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Foremost, I would like to credit His Excellency, our President, kasi tinanong niya noon.

asr-004703
04:22:00.800 --> 04:22:03.040
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kasi I really am very thankful.

asr-004704
04:22:03.220 --> 04:22:15.240
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Sabi niya, bakit ang dami nating, ang EDCOM release na madaming programs na hindi tine-take ng mga estudyante.

asr-004705
04:22:15.460 --> 04:22:17.020
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Bakit ang daming attrition?

asr-004706
04:22:17.380 --> 04:22:18.540
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: That was the question.

asr-004707
04:22:18.680 --> 04:22:20.000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So we came up with the proposal.

asr-004708
04:22:20.380 --> 04:22:23.480
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: The proposal caters the top five

asr-004709
04:22:23.480 --> 04:22:33.140
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Graduates of senior high school who are willing first to enroll to the ten priority programs identified by EDCOM.

asr-004710
04:22:33.140 --> 04:22:38.420
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Number two, they are accepted to a top performing university.

asr-004711
04:22:38.880 --> 04:22:40.740
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May criteria po eh yung university.

asr-004712
04:22:41.160 --> 04:22:44.120
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Whether state university or private.

asr-004713
04:22:44.560 --> 04:22:50.260
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And the student will receive kung private siya, subsidized.

asr-004714
04:22:50.400 --> 04:22:51.920
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Mga 80,000 ba?

asr-004715
04:22:52.000 --> 04:22:53.160
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Can you give me the number?

asr-004716
04:22:53.400 --> 04:22:56.360
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kung private siya, 90,000.

asr-004717
04:22:56.760 --> 04:23:02.240
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kung sa government naman, state university, libre kasi ang tuition fee.

asr-004718
04:23:02.240 --> 04:23:11.400
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: In terms of allowance, ang isang estudyante nakaka-receive ng 45,000 per semester.

asr-004719
04:23:11.400 --> 04:23:14.600
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: For academic year.

asr-004720
04:23:17.300 --> 04:23:17.760
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah.

asr-004721
04:23:17.880 --> 04:23:18.920
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yun po yung ano.

asr-004722
04:23:19.040 --> 04:23:24.800
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Pero ngayon po, of the 20,000 slots for 2026,

asr-004723
04:23:25.020 --> 04:23:28.000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: sa dami ng magagaling na nag-graduate,

asr-004724
04:23:28.000 --> 04:23:32.680
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: we receive already more than 39,000 applicants.

asr-004725
04:23:33.620 --> 04:23:38.880
Rep. Brian Poe: But how do we decide, how do we distribute that, Madam Chair, if I may ask?

asr-004726
04:23:39.380 --> 04:23:41.440
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We have a formula developed.

asr-004727
04:23:42.340 --> 04:23:45.040
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We have a formula developed.

asr-004728
04:23:45.320 --> 04:23:51.040
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So wala pong bahid ng irregularities doon.

asr-004729
04:23:51.040 --> 04:23:57.000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kasi may, based on the grade, based on the per capita income of the students,

asr-004730
04:23:57.000 --> 04:24:03.000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: meron ding point yung siya ay first generation in the family.

asr-004731
04:24:03.040 --> 04:24:03.860
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Ano pa, Cor?

asr-004732
04:24:05.580 --> 04:24:07.000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And then the...

asr-004732-split-1
04:24:14.954 --> 04:24:16.580
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yup.

asr-004732-split-2
04:24:16.580 --> 04:24:17.420
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yup.

asr-004733
04:24:17.520 --> 04:24:17.900
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yup.

asr-004734
04:24:19.960 --> 04:24:20.660
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yup.

asr-004735
04:24:21.480 --> 04:24:28.460
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Proportionately distributed based on the number of graduates of senior high school per region.

asr-004736
04:24:28.460 --> 04:24:30.580
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Na nasa top five.

asr-004737
04:24:30.760 --> 04:24:32.340
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May formula po doon.

asr-004738
04:24:32.980 --> 04:24:35.440
Rep. Brian Poe: So it's truly, it's really merit.

asr-004740
04:24:35.640 --> 04:24:38.200
Rep. Brian Poe: So there's no aspect of economics behind it.

asr-004741
04:24:38.320 --> 04:24:38.680
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po.

asr-004742
04:24:38.800 --> 04:24:39.380
Rep. Brian Poe: Okay.

asr-004743
04:24:39.440 --> 04:24:42.280
Rep. Brian Poe: So it doesn't matter if you're considered poorest of the poor.

asr-004744
04:24:42.420 --> 04:24:46.540
Rep. Brian Poe: You don't necessarily have a leg up over someone else.

asr-004745
04:24:46.580 --> 04:24:47.680
Rep. Brian Poe: It's really based on grades.

asr-004746
04:24:48.120 --> 04:24:52.140
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Zero to two million at least na household income.

asr-004747
04:24:52.440 --> 04:24:54.180
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Irregular family naman hindi naman.

asr-004748
04:24:54.340 --> 04:24:54.900
Rep. Brian Poe: Ah, okay.

asr-004749
04:24:54.980 --> 04:25:00.760
Rep. Brian Poe: So it's only those with zero to, to two million pesos or one million pesos annual income?

asr-004750
04:25:01.000 --> 04:25:01.520
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Hindi naman only po.

asr-004751
04:25:01.600 --> 04:25:07.380
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: But we give priority sa zero to two million income plus grades.

asr-004752
04:25:08.540 --> 04:25:11.580
Rep. Brian Poe: And then do you know the distribution so far?

asr-004753
04:25:11.700 --> 04:25:13.960
Rep. Brian Poe: Where are most of your scholars from currently?

asr-004754
04:25:14.180 --> 04:25:14.420
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po.

asr-004755
04:25:14.520 --> 04:25:15.100
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Meron kami.

asr-004756
04:25:15.320 --> 04:25:20.920
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Because it's easy now to locate because there is an equation and they are generated digitally.

asr-004757
04:25:23.260 --> 04:25:24.220
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: They distribute.

asr-004758
04:25:24.600 --> 04:25:27.060
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So, halimbawa, in Region 1, they have a top performer.

asr-004759
04:25:27.060 --> 04:25:31.900
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: They have a graduate, top performing graduate of 10,000.

asr-004760
04:25:31.960 --> 04:25:33.760
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Region two, they have 5,000.

asr-004761
04:25:34.000 --> 04:25:35.400
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May kanya-kanyang equity.

asr-004762
04:25:35.740 --> 04:25:36.620
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May ratio po.

asr-004763
04:25:37.660 --> 04:25:39.400
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We will provide you copy, Kong.

asr-004764
04:25:39.600 --> 04:25:40.200
Rep. Brian Poe: Sige po.

asr-004765
04:25:40.280 --> 04:25:47.560
Rep. Brian Poe: So moving quickly, I noticed that even with all of this, there is a significant decrease in your budget.

asr-004766
04:25:48.260 --> 04:25:51.800
Rep. Brian Poe: What specific items were hit?

asr-004767
04:25:51.900 --> 04:25:58.120
Rep. Brian Poe: Is there anything in particular that you feel is a critical mistake on the part of the DBM to remove from the budget?

asr-004768
04:26:01.460 --> 04:26:05.060
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We proposed for 70.2 billion kong.

asr-004769
04:26:05.580 --> 04:26:10.620
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And the data, the basis was never a magic based on data.

asr-004770
04:26:11.580 --> 04:26:13.840
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We got 35 billion for NEP.

asr-004771
04:26:14.460 --> 04:26:16.620
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: The gap is 34 billion.

asr-004772
04:26:16.940 --> 04:26:23.000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: In my presentation na kanina, we identified the big ticket na maasasagasaan.

asr-004773
04:26:23.000 --> 04:26:25.920
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: UAQTEA, 29 billion ang kulang.

asr-004774
04:26:26.500 --> 04:26:29.300
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Scholarship, 697 million.

asr-004775
04:26:29.800 --> 04:26:34.340
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yung digital transformation natin namin, sana po ibigay.

asr-004776
04:26:34.380 --> 04:26:37.520
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Masayang yung aming digital system na na-develop.

asr-004777
04:26:37.740 --> 04:26:38.960
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: 331.

asr-004778
04:26:39.800 --> 04:26:43.300
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: 258 million sa monitoring and evaluation function.

asr-004779
04:26:43.700 --> 04:26:46.540
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And the others include many things.

asr-004780
04:26:46.780 --> 04:26:50.860
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So ang total po is 34.8 billion ang kulang.

asr-004781
04:26:50.860 --> 04:26:53.640
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Chair, did I hear that right?

asr-004782
04:26:54.060 --> 04:26:57.160
Rep. Brian Poe: 97 million was lost from scholarships?

asr-004783
04:27:00.120 --> 04:27:02.000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: 697 million po.

asr-004784
04:27:03.060 --> 04:27:05.680
Rep. Brian Poe: 697 million removed from scholarships?

asr-004785
04:27:05.800 --> 04:27:06.700
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po.

asr-004786
04:27:07.240 --> 04:27:09.020
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Ilan ang beneficiary?

asr-004787
04:27:11.080 --> 04:27:11.940
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po.

asr-004788
04:27:12.460 --> 04:27:16.560
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And then we can submit to you the breakdown of this.

asr-004789
04:27:16.840 --> 04:27:17.500
Rep. Brian Poe: Okay.

asr-004790
04:27:17.600 --> 04:27:23.020
Rep. Brian Poe: Just wanted to highlight that, Madam Chair, so that maybe we can look into these scholarships that were removed.

asr-004791
04:27:23.080 --> 04:27:28.600
Rep. Brian Poe: And ask the question as to why these scholarships were removed when the students are very deserving.

asr-004792
04:27:29.160 --> 04:27:35.160
Rep. Brian Poe: Again, moving along quickly, we want to make sure that our education is competitive.

asr-004793
04:27:35.160 --> 04:27:40.400
Rep. Brian Poe: And that it will remain competitive, especially in the age of artificial intelligence.

asr-004794
04:27:41.040 --> 04:27:45.320
Rep. Brian Poe: I believe that you have created an AI roadmap.

asr-004795
04:27:45.860 --> 04:27:48.880
Rep. Brian Poe: Where are we in that roadmap currently?

asr-004796
04:27:48.880 --> 04:27:55.260
Rep. Brian Poe: And what, what are we funding in the 2027 GAA to support our AI programs and initiatives?

asr-004797
04:27:56.700 --> 04:27:57.980
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Nasaan yung listahan?

asr-004798
04:27:58.100 --> 04:27:59.320
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes, sir.

asr-004799
04:28:00.840 --> 04:28:02.660
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We are aware of that.

asr-004800
04:28:02.920 --> 04:28:06.480
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: The, what's that?

asr-004801
04:28:06.640 --> 04:28:11.340
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Adoption of AI technology comes faster than the policy.

asr-004802
04:28:11.340 --> 04:28:17.300
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And comes faster than the capacity building among SUCs.

asr-004803
04:28:17.300 --> 04:28:24.840
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So to control that at least, we came up already with the National AI in Higher Education Policy.

asr-004804
04:28:25.260 --> 04:28:26.280
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Meron na po kami.

asr-004805
04:28:26.280 --> 04:28:31.180
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And now we are now cascading to state university and colleges, including HEI.

asr-004806
04:28:31.180 --> 04:28:38.400
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: That they must come up with an AI policy to avoid, what's that?

asr-004807
04:28:38.700 --> 04:28:44.100
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Denuding the human thinking capacity of our students.

asr-004808
04:28:44.100 --> 04:28:52.280
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And in order to, and we focus on this priority to really capacitate our teachers, faculty.

asr-004809
04:28:52.560 --> 04:28:54.280
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So we funded already.

asr-004810
04:28:54.280 --> 04:29:02.300
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Several programs cascaded it to different state university po.

asr-004811
04:29:02.300 --> 04:29:07.880
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And total is, hindi lang five million.

asr-004812
04:29:08.160 --> 04:29:15.300
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yung total na in-locate namin, may AI in health sciences application.

asr-004813
04:29:16.180 --> 04:29:18.400
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May AI in financial literacy.

asr-004814
04:29:18.980 --> 04:29:20.580
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May AI in fishing.

asr-004815
04:29:21.020 --> 04:29:22.660
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May AI in agriculture.

asr-004816
04:29:23.340 --> 04:29:27.480
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So while we are crafting the massive manpower development for AI.

asr-004817
04:29:28.900 --> 04:29:32.800
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Chair, I want to highlight the fact that CHED is taking the initiative on this.

asr-004818
04:29:32.800 --> 04:29:35.420
Rep. Brian Poe: And that their framework is actually pretty much done already.

asr-004819
04:29:35.420 --> 04:29:37.100
Rep. Brian Poe: And being cascaded.

asr-004820
04:29:37.100 --> 04:29:41.940
Rep. Brian Poe: Tayo. Hindi pa pumapasang AI framework natin dito sa House.

asr-004821
04:29:42.060 --> 04:29:45.220
Rep. Brian Poe: That bill is still not yet with the Senate.

asr-004822
04:29:45.220 --> 04:29:47.220
Rep. Brian Poe: And I hope we can catch up to CHED.

asr-004823
04:29:47.220 --> 04:29:50.580
Rep. Brian Poe: But that brings up an important note.

asr-004824
04:29:50.900 --> 04:29:52.000
Rep. Brian Poe: May I ask?

asr-004825
04:29:52.060 --> 04:29:53.360
Rep. Brian Poe: Because I've been going through your budget.

asr-004826
04:29:53.360 --> 04:29:54.280
Rep. Brian Poe: And I haven't noticed.

asr-004827
04:29:54.460 --> 04:29:57.940
Rep. Brian Poe: There seems to be no budget for research and development.

asr-004828
04:29:58.280 --> 04:29:58.720
Rep. Brian Poe: No.

asr-004829
04:29:58.860 --> 04:29:59.500
Rep. Brian Poe: And.

asr-004830
04:29:59.500 --> 04:30:05.640
Rep. Brian Poe: I want the committee to take note that CHED's mission is not just to have students graduate.

asr-004831
04:30:06.060 --> 04:30:07.800
Rep. Brian Poe: It's also capacity building.

asr-004832
04:30:08.040 --> 04:30:08.920
Rep. Brian Poe: It's also innovation.

asr-004833
04:30:09.280 --> 04:30:14.840
Rep. Brian Poe: It's also furthering research and development because that is also the job of the academe.

asr-004834
04:30:14.900 --> 04:30:24.300
Rep. Brian Poe: You look at universities around the world, and they contribute to the development of their countries through research and development in higher education.

asr-004835
04:30:24.720 --> 04:30:27.460
Rep. Brian Poe: So I want to know if there's a budget here for that.

asr-004836
04:30:30.000 --> 04:30:30.980
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We have.

asr-004837
04:30:31.060 --> 04:30:31.660
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We focus.

asr-004838
04:30:31.780 --> 04:30:35.660
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: This is one of our priority area under our Achieve agenda.

asr-004839
04:30:36.100 --> 04:30:45.520
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: It is represented in letter C, centralized, harmonized SDG base, R&amp;D agenda.

asr-004840
04:30:46.160 --> 04:30:52.460
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We focus on the 17 SDG, and we already have several initiatives here.

asr-004841
04:30:53.300 --> 04:30:55.440
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: We will submit it to you.

asr-004842
04:30:55.440 --> 04:30:58.080
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: But as to the funding, as to the funding,

asr-004843
04:30:58.860 --> 04:31:00.040
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: the funding,

asr-004844
04:31:00.040 --> 04:31:05.940
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: that we included in our proposal is the capacity building of faculty researchers.

asr-004845
04:31:05.940 --> 04:31:10.980
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: But as to the project itself, we lodge it to HEDF.

asr-004846
04:31:11.560 --> 04:31:17.780
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So marami na po kami mga indicative application on the research.

asr-004847
04:31:17.940 --> 04:31:19.540
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So nandun po sa HEDF.

asr-004848
04:31:19.740 --> 04:31:33.180
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: In fact, if time may allow me, we have, yeah, we allotted 1.4 billion from the HEDF pillars funded project po.

asr-004849
04:31:33.260 --> 04:31:39.260
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: It's 15% of the total program that we allotted from HEDF.

asr-004850
04:31:40.440 --> 04:31:41.300
Rep. Brian Poe: Thank you.

asr-004851
04:31:41.400 --> 04:31:46.340
Rep. Brian Poe: I bring that up because our chair here came from research.

asr-004852
04:31:46.640 --> 04:31:50.260
Rep. Brian Poe: And in fact, my first job in government was as a researcher.

asr-004853
04:31:50.800 --> 04:31:57.660
Rep. Brian Poe: So I do believe that funding research and developing it is very important for the development of our entire nation.

asr-004854
04:31:57.660 --> 04:32:01.300
Rep. Brian Poe: And keeping us competitive in an age of artificial intelligence.

asr-004855
04:32:01.300 --> 04:32:02.520
Rep. Brian Poe: And innovation.

asr-004856
04:32:02.980 --> 04:32:06.280
Rep. Brian Poe: So hopefully, we can continue to fund those programs.

asr-004857
