asr-005837
05:31:40.460 --> 05:31:48.880
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Institutional recognition is based on their compliance on the criteria sa, we set, like COPC and among others.

asr-005838
05:31:49.340 --> 05:31:56.580
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: So ibig sabihin, Madam Chair, itong mga may institutional recognition lang po ang masasabi nating covered ng free higher education.

asr-005839
05:31:58.140 --> 05:32:02.440
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Unfortunately, with a heavy heart, yes po.

asr-005840
05:32:02.440 --> 05:32:14.040
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: At kung atin po silang tutulungan na maka-comply sa requirements ng institutional recognition, sila po ay mapagbibigyan sa free higher education.

asr-005841
05:32:14.620 --> 05:32:22.840
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po, that's the developmental part of our Commission on Higher Education. Pero, yes po.

asr-005842
05:32:23.280 --> 05:32:26.700
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Tinanong ko po yun, Madam Chair, paalala lang po sa mga kasamahan namin

asr-005843
05:32:26.700 --> 05:32:40.040
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: na kung atin pang tutulungan, atin pang lilinangin. Kasi ang gusto naman natin, access talaga, e talagang kailangan pa natin mas tignan pa yung additional space or fiscal space

asr-005844
05:32:40.040 --> 05:32:47.520
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: para sa posibleng pag-accommodate sa ating mga mag-aaral galing sa LUC.

asr-005845
05:32:48.200 --> 05:32:56.840
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Pero Madam Chair, habang paparami po yung LUC, may recommendation po ba kayo sa Kongreso para paano natin mamamanage itong ating mga LUCs ngayon?

asr-005846
05:32:58.080 --> 05:33:00.520
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Thank you for asking that, Kong Jude.

asr-005847
05:33:00.520 --> 05:33:04.740
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Now, in fact, this is one of the major challenges in higher education.

asr-005848
05:33:04.740 --> 05:33:10.340
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Because the offering, first is the offering of the local universities and colleges.

asr-005849
05:33:10.640 --> 05:33:13.620
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: They go beyond what is mandated by law.

asr-005850
05:33:14.220 --> 05:33:21.520
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Sometimes they overlap with the offerings of recognized state universities and colleges within the region.

asr-005851
05:33:21.520 --> 05:33:26.340
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: To the extent of offering masteral and PhD degree program.

asr-005852
05:33:26.340 --> 05:33:33.520
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So ngayon sa side ng CHED, gumawa na po kami ng guidelines for consultation

asr-005853
05:33:33.520 --> 05:33:55.000
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And with the oversight of Commissioner Mitz, we are now trying to instill policy reform para po makontrol at maiwasan ang mushrooming ng local universities and colleges.

asr-005854
05:33:55.000 --> 05:33:56.700
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Because it gives

asr-005855
05:33:56.700 --> 05:33:58.520
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: many, many effect.

asr-005856
05:33:58.980 --> 05:34:07.640
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: In fact, mas madaling dumami ang local universities and colleges than state universities and colleges, Kong.

asr-005857
05:34:07.800 --> 05:34:10.060
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Thank you, Madam Chair, for all those points.

asr-005858
05:34:10.320 --> 05:34:17.920
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Last point ko na lang po, Madam Chair, is for the last probably about four hours, we've all discussed.

asr-005859
05:34:18.240 --> 05:34:18.920
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Six hours.

asr-005860
05:34:18.920 --> 05:34:19.540
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Six hours.

asr-005861
05:34:19.760 --> 05:34:23.680
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: We've been discussing about mostly SUCs, no?

asr-005862
05:34:23.960 --> 05:34:26.820
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: But if you look at the data you've given us, Madam Chair,

asr-005864
05:34:27.040 --> 05:34:31.980
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: and this is just a manifestation, more than half of our students are actually

asr-005865
05:34:31.980 --> 05:34:37.520
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: enrolled in private schools. Maybe in the coming years, because we've seen, Madam

asr-005866
05:34:37.520 --> 05:34:43.600
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Chair, how much change and leadership you've given, you have shown in CHED that

asr-005867
05:34:43.600 --> 05:34:48.620
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: has produced significant accomplishments since you've been here last year. So

asr-005868
05:34:48.620 --> 05:34:54.920
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: we're looking forward that we can also make such, we can also take, we can also

asr-005869
05:34:54.920 --> 05:34:59.720
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: undertake such interventions also to address the concerns of our private

asr-005870
05:34:59.720 --> 05:35:03.820
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: schools where more than half of our college students are actually enrolled,

asr-005871
05:35:04.000 --> 05:35:04.400
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Madam Chair.

asr-005871-split-1
05:35:05.100 --> 05:35:08.600
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah, we take note of that seriously, Kong. And thank you for that

asr-005872
05:35:08.600 --> 05:35:10.660
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: words of support and appreciation.

asr-005872-split-1
05:35:10.660 --> 05:35:13.380
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: So that's all, Madam Chair. I would like to

asr-005873
05:35:13.380 --> 05:35:19.100
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: reiterate once again my commitment to support the budget of the Commission on

asr-005874
05:35:19.100 --> 05:35:25.120
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: Higher Education. And knowing, Madam Chair, of what more needs to be funded,

asr-005875
05:35:25.200 --> 05:35:30.460
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: I hope we can rally on our colleagues to really push for the increase

asr-005876
05:35:30.460 --> 05:35:34.560
Rep. Jude A. Acidre: of the Commission on Higher Education's budget.

asr-005876-split-1
05:35:36.860 --> 05:35:39.580
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Thank you, Kong Jude Acidre.

asr-005877
05:35:39.720 --> 05:35:48.220
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: And that concludes the list of members of the House who would want to interpellate or

asr-005878
05:35:48.220 --> 05:35:56.820
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: ask questions towards our CHED family. We will suspend in the meantime to wait for

asr-005879
05:35:56.820 --> 05:36:02.380
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: the honorable chairperson of the committee who is just finishing up but

asr-005880
05:36:02.380 --> 05:36:10.320
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: will soon be on her way. So, while we, while we suspend, you can breathe a little

asr-005881
05:36:10.320 --> 05:36:22.340
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: already, ma'am, and eat. Medyo hindi pa nakakain ng maayos. Please have your lunch. Snack pa lang po ang kinain nyo while we wait for our

asr-005882
05:36:22.340 --> 05:36:26.480
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: chairperson. So, we suspend in the meantime this briefing.

asr-005891
07:34:32.820 --> 07:34:35.760
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: So we now resume this budget briefing.

asr-005892
07:34:35.760 --> 07:34:43.960
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: And we recognize our chair, Chair Mikaela Angela B. Suansing, for just a few questions.

asr-005893
07:34:53.120 --> 07:34:54.600
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Good evening, everyone.

asr-005894
07:34:54.940 --> 07:34:56.860
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I'm so sorry to keep everyone waiting.

asr-005895
07:34:56.900 --> 07:35:05.660
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I came from the DILG Budget Hearing, the PCSO, so medyo tumatakbo everywhere.

asr-005896
07:35:06.800 --> 07:35:11.040
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So I just wanted to pose a few questions.

asr-005897
07:35:11.040 --> 07:35:19.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Siguro, Chair Shirley, baka po naitanong na ito. Pero I just wanted to, I guess, summarize at the end of the day.

asr-005898
07:35:19.080 --> 07:35:26.900
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Sir, the most important thing I would like to ask on, kasi po, isa po ito sa mga pinakamalilaki nating pinondohan last year,

asr-005899
07:35:26.900 --> 07:35:34.780
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: would be the status of the release of the FHE for payment of deficiency to SUC.

asr-005900
07:35:34.780 --> 07:35:40.680
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, last year po, how we went about it, Chair Shirley, and thank you for working with us on this.

asr-005901
07:35:40.680 --> 07:35:50.060
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: It was 12 billion in total, roughly, 7.5 billion sourced from the Higher Education Development Fund,

asr-005902
07:35:50.060 --> 07:35:54.780
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and roughly 4.8 billion sourced from the GAA.

asr-005903
07:35:54.980 --> 07:36:01.340
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So I just wanted to request po siguro an update as to how that's going about,

asr-005904
07:36:01.340 --> 07:36:18.180
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: because hinihintay din po ng ating mga state universities and colleges yun pong pambayad doon po sa kakulangan sa implementation po ng Higher Free Tertiary Education Law nitong mga nakaraang taon.

asr-005906
07:36:19.220 --> 07:36:23.600
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah, thank you very much, ma'am. Good evening, Chair, and congratulations.

asr-005907
07:36:24.660 --> 07:36:27.760
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: And thank you for waiting. Thank you to the baby.

asr-005908
07:36:28.900 --> 07:36:36.840
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes, ma'am. We already signed a joint memorandum circular with DBM and CHED.

asr-005909
07:36:37.040 --> 07:36:47.500
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So two weeks ago, if I am not mistaken, they released already 9.7 billion for the deficiency.

asr-005910
07:36:48.140 --> 07:37:04.140
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Hindi na po namin, yan nandiyan na po. And we are processing now. In fact, na-release na yung mga iba. Marami nang nagpasalamat sa unang 108 SUCs na mabibigyan namin.

asr-005911
07:37:04.140 --> 07:37:07.440
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May mga hindi pa nabigyan.

asr-005912
07:37:07.440 --> 07:37:21.600
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kasi they lack the requirements pa, pero we will make sure that upon compliance of the requirement, ibibigay naman po sa total na hinihingi nila and subjected for, that was subjected na na-validate na.

asr-005913
07:37:21.980 --> 07:37:27.920
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Chair Shirley. Just wanted to clarify po because roughly 12 billion pesos po yun, diba?

asr-005914
07:37:28.020 --> 07:37:47.700
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I'm looking at the status that was given just now. 9.4 billion allocated for those with deficient billings from 2022 to 2024. Without submission is just 341 million.

asr-005915
07:37:49.080 --> 07:37:57.360
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Pwede ko po pang tanungin kasi po, that adds up to just roughly 9.7 billion.

asr-005916
07:37:58.340 --> 07:38:01.860
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: 12 billion. So nasan po yung remainder? The remainder of the 12 billion?

asr-005917
07:38:02.300 --> 07:38:03.560
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Nasa Bureau of Treasury.

asr-005918
07:38:04.220 --> 07:38:16.580
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So kanino po mapupunta tayo? Dito po sa first cluster na may deficiency, doon po sa walang submission? Kasi po if we add it all up, hindi po nag-add up eh.

asr-005919
07:38:18.260 --> 07:38:25.140
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Itong 9.7 kasi, ito po, initially 12.7 billion ang na-compute natin.

asr-005920
07:38:26.320 --> 07:38:28.260
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Because, can you help me here?

asr-005921
07:38:28.500 --> 07:38:39.060
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Because of the faculty-student ratio. And then there was a little discrepancy of the, the submission by SUC.

asr-005922
07:38:39.140 --> 07:38:49.360
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So sabi namin, we need to stick to the initial submission because if this deficiency had been paid on time, yun ang natuloy.

asr-005923
07:38:49.440 --> 07:38:56.560
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So we did not entertain any more additional claims po.

asr-005924
07:38:57.340 --> 07:38:59.580
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So, can Ma'am Alma?

asr-005925
07:39:01.420 --> 07:39:07.240
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So, as of this date, 9.7 billion. No more claims. Additional?

asr-005926
07:39:14.100 --> 07:39:14.780
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: 108.

asr-005927
07:39:15.660 --> 07:39:25.360
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: 108 SUCs na po kasi ang nag-submit. That covers the 9.7 billion. And we are counting 113.

asr-005928
07:39:27.560 --> 07:39:32.280
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: But, sir po kasi, Chair, even if you add the

asr-005929
07:39:32.280 --> 07:39:50.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: The 97 account for the 9.4 billion, 97 SUCs, 11 SUCs account for the 341. So at 9.7 billion, that only accounts for 108 of the SUCs.

asr-005930
07:39:50.240 --> 07:40:01.520
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So how about the remainder? May nakikita din po ako dito na may 8. There are 8 without any deficiencies. So that only adds up to 116.

asr-005931
07:40:01.520 --> 07:40:03.240
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: How about the other SUCs po?

asr-005932
07:40:09.540 --> 07:40:14.940
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: May mga chair? May mga SUC kasi na walang deficiency.

asr-005933
07:40:15.600 --> 07:40:16.200
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po.

asr-005934
07:40:16.300 --> 07:40:21.800
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: At may mga SUC na overpayment. Overpaid. So hindi po sila nakasali.

asr-005935
07:40:22.580 --> 07:40:33.380
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So ito na lang. Kung ang hinahanap nyo po is hindi na maximize yung inalot natin na 7.8 billion. Totoo po yun.

asr-005936
07:40:33.960 --> 07:40:36.940
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kasi 9 points sa HEDF yun na iwan.

asr-005937
07:40:37.140 --> 07:40:39.140
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: I-exhaust namin lahat.

asr-005938
07:40:39.200 --> 07:40:40.360
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Ang yata ang ginawa

asr-005939
07:40:40.360 --> 07:40:52.560
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: ni DBM is in-exhaust lahat yung 4 point something billion galing sa Congress, sa GAA. And then yung na iwan is yung sa HEDF.

asr-005940
07:40:52.660 --> 07:41:04.720
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: So, GAA 4.4, tapos yung HEDF 5.2 billion kaya 9.7 lang. So in short, may naiwan na about 2 billion sa HEDF.

asr-005941
07:41:05.020 --> 07:41:10.220
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So our plan, the intent po is we will no longer be spending that

asr-005942
07:41:10.220 --> 07:41:12.300
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: 2 billion in the HEDF.

asr-005943
07:41:12.360 --> 07:41:13.040
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: For the deficiency?

asr-005944
07:41:13.540 --> 07:41:13.880
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes po.

asr-005945
07:41:14.180 --> 07:41:16.080
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Wala na po kasi wala ng submission.

asr-005946
07:41:16.440 --> 07:41:16.960
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Am I correct?

asr-005947
07:41:17.380 --> 07:41:17.960
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes.

asr-005948
07:41:18.080 --> 07:41:18.480
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Okay.

asr-005949
07:41:19.830 --> 07:41:20.030
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Opo.

asr-005950
07:41:20.390 --> 07:41:30.120
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Chair Shirley, very, very important lang for us to align on this point because once we deliberate on the budget of the state universities and colleges,

asr-005951
07:41:30.440 --> 07:41:36.840
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I just want to be able to face them and say that we've taken care of our commitment to them as promised.

asr-005952
07:41:36.840 --> 07:41:41.700
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So hopefully po when we do the budget deliberations with the SUCs,

asr-005953
07:41:41.700 --> 07:41:48.700
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I really do hope no one will come forward and say we were not accommodated in terms of our deficiency.

asr-005954
07:41:48.700 --> 07:41:50.580
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We delivered our promise.

asr-005955
07:41:50.580 --> 07:42:00.180
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Okay. Sige, Chair Shirley. Thank you. I really, I just really, really needed that assurance, because, alam mo naman, Chair Shirley,

asr-005956
07:42:00.180 --> 07:42:10.240
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: grabe yung ginawa nating hirap last year, mabuo lang po yung 12 billion na yun para po sa kabayaran sa mga deficient.

asr-005957
07:42:10.760 --> 07:42:17.640
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, yeah, I just want to give the assurance, of course, I'm sure the state universities and colleges are watching us today,

asr-005958
07:42:17.860 --> 07:42:34.440
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: closely monitoring today's deliberations, so I will hold on to the assurance of Chair Shirley that we no longer have any deficiencies unpaid for 2000, as of 2000, on process pa.

asr-005959
07:42:34.600 --> 07:42:40.220
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yeah, on process yung mga iba, kasi yung mga nagla-late submission ng mga additional requirements.

asr-005960
07:42:40.700 --> 07:42:46.460
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: But, upon submission kong Chair, mababayaran sila lahat.

asr-005961
07:42:46.460 --> 07:42:54.640
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Chair Shirley, may I ask, what would be the commitment? Like, by when would all the deficiencies be settled?

asr-005962
07:42:54.640 --> 07:43:03.560
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Because, siguro po, the terminology, the terminology that a lot of people don't really want to hear is on process.

asr-005963
07:43:03.600 --> 07:43:09.660
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, pwede po ba naming matanong, ano po yung commitment? Kailan po ma-disperse lahat po ng mga kabayaran?

asr-005964
07:43:09.660 --> 07:43:12.040
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Kailan sa mga state universities and colleges?

asr-005965
07:43:12.360 --> 07:43:15.240
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Third week September, po. At mosque.

asr-005966
07:43:15.520 --> 07:43:20.360
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Kung sabihin niyo po sa kanila, Chair, na kung hindi sila mag-submit, kasalanan na nila.

asr-005967
07:43:20.720 --> 07:43:21.200
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Okay.

asr-005968
07:43:23.540 --> 07:43:24.260
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Medyo...

asr-005969
07:43:24.260 --> 07:43:25.740
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Chair, bawal magsungit na.

asr-005970
07:43:25.740 --> 07:43:28.260
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Ay, hindi na. Nakangiti pa naman ako.

asr-005971
07:43:28.260 --> 07:43:32.340
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Okay. So, ang commitment po ng Chair ay third week of September.

asr-005972
07:43:32.340 --> 07:43:35.240
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Third week of September. Huwag niyo naman ako yung pahiya dito.

asr-005973
07:43:35.240 --> 07:43:35.700
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Yes.

asr-005974
07:43:35.700 --> 07:43:37.780
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Third week of September.

asr-005975
07:43:37.780 --> 07:43:41.040
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I'm just saying that's a really serendipitous...

asr-005976
07:43:41.040 --> 07:43:46.980
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: ...target, only because that is the timeline for the plenary deliberation.

asr-005977
07:43:46.980 --> 07:43:52.380
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, medyo week of reckoning din yun. Magsasabay ulit ang CHED at SUCs.

asr-005978
07:43:52.860 --> 07:43:55.500
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Magkasunod po kayo parate sa plenary deliberation.

asr-005979
07:43:55.720 --> 07:44:02.420
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, please, please, please po. Para din po kay Chair Shirley who committed,

asr-005980
07:44:03.180 --> 07:44:10.180
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I would like to request the CHED family to please help Chair Shirley adhere to the commitment.

asr-005981
07:44:10.520 --> 07:44:14.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Dahil makikita-kita po tayo along with the SUCs in the plenary.

asr-005982
07:44:14.380 --> 07:44:23.280
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, we don't want it to remain an issue come plenary because plenary will start around September 14.

asr-005983
07:44:23.560 --> 07:44:29.540
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, until the 25th. So, papasok po siya dun sa third week of September.

asr-005984
07:44:29.780 --> 07:44:31.240
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Saktong-sakto talaga siya dun.

asr-005985
07:44:31.560 --> 07:44:32.140
CHED Chairperson Shirley Castañeda Agrupis: Okay.

asr-005986
07:44:33.440 --> 07:44:35.220
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Next question, Chair Shirley.

